== 1. WHY THIS IS A SPECIFICATION AND NOT A DIFF ==

Both files exist and both are edited in the middle, so a diff would need their
surrounding lines quoted verbatim, and this session is forbidden to read them. A
policy document is the worst possible case for guessed context: its indentation
and key order carry no semantics but do decide whether a hunk applies, so an
invented context line produces either a loud rejection or a hunk applied to the
wrong tier - and the wrong tier here is the family one.

So this file states, for each edit, exactly which key gains exactly which value,
and states separately and explicitly which key must NOT change. There is no
index line and no blob hash, because neither can be derived from a description.

ON ONE PLACEHOLDER, AND WHY IT IS A PLACEHOLDER. The family classification's key
appears below as <FAMILY_CLASSIFICATION>. It resolves to the key the target
repository's policy document spells for the tier whose egress set is empty - the
one carrying household content. It is deliberately not written out here: this
repository is public, and contract 12 section 4.4.3 holds that no artifact of
this tier names, counts, summarizes or points at that content. Substitute it when
applying, by reading the row in the policy document - which section 4 asks you to
do anyway, and with your own eyes rather than through a test result.

== 2. WHAT MUST NOT CHANGE ==

This is the one change in the series that WIDENS what may leave the machine.
Everything below is the boundary on that widening, and the first item is the
whole reason the boundary exists.

  1. THE FAMILY CLASSIFICATION KEEPS AN EMPTY EGRESS SET. Not a narrowed set, not
     a set containing the bus, not a set containing anything: empty. That tier
     never becomes eligible for any target, and its content is excluded from the
     deployment entirely rather than filtered on the way out.

     Exclusion, not filtering, is the point. A filter is code that runs on every
     item and has to be right every time; an empty egress set is a property of
     the data's classification that no code path can widen. If you find yourself
     adding the bus to this row to make something work, the something is wrong,
     not the row.

  2. signalbus IS NOT ADDED TO ANY OF THE FIVE EXISTING TIERS. In particular not
     to strict_local, which is where financial figures, health signals and
     journal text live. Content in an existing tier reaches the bus only by
     first being reduced to a directional signal in one of the two NEW tiers -
     and that reduction is a deliberate act at a call site, not a permission
     granted by the matrix.

  3. THE FIVE EXISTING TIERS KEEP THEIR CURRENT TARGETS. This change adds; it
     removes nothing and renames nothing.

  4. THE EVALUATION FUNCTION IS NOT CHANGED. Whatever answers "is this egress
     blocked", it keeps its logic. The new rows flow through it exactly as the
     existing rows do. A new special case for the bus would be a second policy
     engine, and two policy engines disagree eventually.

  5. NO PAYLOAD FIELD IS ADDED. The envelope in section 3.3 is the whole of what
     may travel. It has no field for a balance, a due date, an account
     identifier or free text over 120 characters, and the correct way to keep it
     that way is that THE FIELD DOES NOT EXIST.

